<title>GERMANY: Thyssen Industrie 95/96 group net falls.</title>
<headline>Thyssen Industrie 95/96 group net falls.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Sept 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   65	vs 104</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     148     vs 194</p>
<p>    Group income from ord. activities    239     vs 194</p>
<p>    Group sales				  9,147   vs 8,497</p>
<p>    Dividend				     4.80    vs 6 marks</p>
<p>    Incoming orders			    9,708   vs 10,087</p>
<p>    Work force (average)		     42,217  vs 42,511</p>
<p>    Personnel costs			    3,464   vs 3,382</p>
<p>    Cash flow				    392     vs 463</p>
<p>    Investments				  493     vs 404</p>
<p>NOTE - Thyssen Industrie AG chairman Eckhard Rohkamm, in remarks prepared for delivery to the annual news conference, forecast the company would post group income from ordinary activities over 250 million marks in the current business year and 350 million marks next year.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn Newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
